  "title": "endpoint_dialog: small preference-fetching code cleanup.",
  "description": "Fetch the ip.conv_agg_flag preference value with prefs_get_bool_value(),\nafter getting the pref_t for that preference with\nprefs_find_preference().\n\nThat means we fetch a Boolean preference with the right routine, and\nthat we only fetch a pointer to the \"ip\" preferences module once (rather\nthan finding it and then, in a call to prefs_get_uint_value(), finding\nit again - prefs_find_preference() checks whether it's handed a null\nmodule pointer and, if so, returns null).",
